WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.320
Between roles like Harley Quinn, Tonya&nbsp;
Harding, and Sharon Tate — when you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.200
a part that requires an iconic diva, you call&nbsp;
Margot Robbie. But what happened on the set of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.080
The Wolf of Wall Street that was too much even&nbsp;
for this megastar? Keep watching to find out.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.160
During production on The Wolf of Wall Street,&nbsp;
Margot Robbie joined a long list of actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.760
who filmed love scenes they eventually regretted.&nbsp;
Playing Naomi Lapaglia, the fictional second wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:29.840
of millionaire stockbroker Jordan Belfort,&nbsp;
Robbie filmed a variety of sensual scenes.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.463
“You don’t wanna be my friend?”

00:00:33.463 --> 00:00:36.800
“We’re not gonna be friends.”

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.400
However, the scene that most stood out&nbsp;
for the Australian actress was one where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.040
Naomi and Jordan, played by Leonardo&nbsp;
Dicaprio, make love on a bed of cash.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.400
Like most film productions, fake&nbsp;
cash was used to film the scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.520
and the bills — produced by famed movie&nbsp;
moneymaker RJR Props — left Robbie with an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.360
unusual cautionary tale to share. In a 2017&nbsp;
interview with The Daily Beast, she warned:

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.320
"I got a million paper cuts on my back from all&nbsp;
that money! It's not as glamorous as it sounds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.080
If anyone is ever planning on having&nbsp;
sex on top of a pile of cash: don't."

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.280
Yep, you heard that right! Robbie suffered&nbsp;
battle scars from rolling around in money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.640
Apparently the texture of movie money&nbsp;
is different from the real thing, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.560
everyone on set that day found out exactly&nbsp;
how much of a difference a small change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.880
in texture can make. In her interview&nbsp;
with The Daily Beast, Robbie reflected:

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.080
"Maybe real money is a bit softer,&nbsp;
but the fake money is like paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.000
and when I got up off the bed, I turned&nbsp;
around to get my robe and everyone gasped.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.800
I said, 'What is it?' And they&nbsp;
said, 'You look like you've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.640
whipped a million times. Your back is&nbsp;
covered in a thousand red scratches.'"

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.800
If only that was the height of excitement&nbsp;
during Robbie’s Wolf of Wall Street experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.640
Turns out, Margot Robbie's uncomfortable&nbsp;
love scene with co-star Leonardo DiCaprio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.560
was one of many that stuck with her after&nbsp;
the cameras stopped rolling. The Wolf of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.200
Wall Street star also revealed to The Daily&nbsp;
Beast which scene was the most bonkers to film:

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.400
"Every single scene was absolutely insane.&nbsp;
Definitely the Quaalude scene. I remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.760
sitting there going, 'I will never,&nbsp;
ever film a scene like this again.'"

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.440
We doubt you’ve forgotten this once-in-a-lifetime&nbsp;
sequence, but if you need a refresher:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.360
the “Quaalude scene” occurs in the hectic&nbsp;
final act of The Wolf of Wall Street,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.760
when Jordan drives out to his country club to&nbsp;
make an important call. While on the phone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.080
he discovers the seemingly-expired Quaaludes&nbsp;
he took with Jonah Hill’s Donnie, were,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.880
in fact, still active. As the effects of the&nbsp;
drugs kick in, Jordan realizes his shady business&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.440
dealings have gotten him in serious trouble,&nbsp;
and he springs into action to get himself out.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.760
Over the course of a hysterical 10 minutes,&nbsp;
an extremely high Jordan crawls his way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.920
back to his car, drives home, yells at an&nbsp;
equally high Donnie for double-crossing him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.440
and then saves Donnie as he starts&nbsp;
choking to death on a piece of ham.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.520
Meanwhile, a pregnant Naomi is left&nbsp;
to watch and worry. It's no wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.200
the scene left such a big impression on&nbsp;
Robbie. She recalled to The Daily Beast:

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.520
"I'm sitting there [as Naomi], eight months&nbsp;
pregnant, and Leo and Jonah are crawling around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.160
trying to strangle each other and I had to try&nbsp;
not to laugh because they looked so ridiculous."

